From 5aee8e535490abc699e157df6ba268cae47b205e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crindo18 <chrisjohnalado@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 02:36:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] M3 review: fix a system-comparison confound, remove the
 runtime bottleneck

BLOCKING: enhancedConfig derived from defaultConfig, so it kept the 21x21
peak neighbourhood after baselineConfig moved to 17x17. The two systems
were about to be compared with different peak geometry - baseline ceiling
27.8 peaks/s with a binding density cap, enhanced 18.2 with an inert one.
Enhancement 1 is a claim about peak SELECTION; measuring it against a
different peak NEIGHBOURHOOD confounds the two and nothing could have been
concluded. enhancedConfig now derives from baselineConfig; new
tSystemParity asserts every shared field. Discard any enhanced index or
result built before this.

Runtime: synthesizeQuery called setupPaths() twice per query (directly for
the noise path, and via resolveProcPath). setupPaths runs addpath over
genpath(src) every time and invalidates MATLAB's function cache. Measured
4,300x slower than needed - 2000 calls take 46.7 s vs 0.011 s. That is
98% of the subset run's wall clock (0.373 s/query against a 0.0069 s
median match time). New projectRoot() memoises the root; every hot path
uses it.

Headroom: computeMetrics now reports normScoreMedian, normScoreP05,
marginMedian and marginMin. New s06b_findKnee sweeps SNR below 0 dB to
locate where the baseline actually degrades - the M3 subset returned
100.0% in every cell including 3 s at 0 dB, which leaves success
criterion 1 (a 10 pp gain at 0 dB) unreachable. Not a bug: peak survival
at 0 dB is ~12%, but a dozen surviving hashes still beat 99 rivals on a
100-song database. Analysis and options in docs/designNotes.md.
